  user_input {
    user_response: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the html\n\nGoogle AI Studio Full-Stack Build Prompt\n\nYou are an expert full-stack Python and React developer. Take the exported UI prototype from Google Stitch and build a complete, runnable full-stack application for Bootcamp Commute Sync using a FastAPI backend and a React + Tailwind CSS frontend.\n\n1. Backend Requirements (FastAPI)\n\nCreate a clean, modular FastAPI backend (main.py) with CORS enabled and automatic Swagger UI (/docs):\n\nLive Event Scraper & Fallback (scraper.py):\n\nWrite an async function using httpx and BeautifulSoup4 to fetch https://promptwars.in/bootcamp.html.\n\nExtract upcoming Bootcamp cities (e.g., Bengaluru, Gurugram), session schedules (Morning Session: 9:00 AM - 1:00 PM, Evening Session: 2:00 PM - 6:00 PM), and program details.\n\nInclude robust fallback/seed data so the app works seamlessly even if the external page structure changes or is offline.\n\nDatabase & Models (models.py using SQLite + SQLModel):\n\nEvent: id, city, title, date_str, session_label, start_time, venue_area, nearest_venue_stop.\n\nCityArea: id, city, area_name, transit_stop, transit_type (Metro | Bus), common_meetup_point. (Pre-seed realistic areas and transit stops for Bengaluru and Gurugram).\n\nCommuteRSVP: id, user_token (unique UUID string), attendee_name, event_id, area_id, boarding_time, is_joining (boolean), updated_at.\n\nREST API Endpoints:\n\nGET /api/events \342\200\224 Returns upcoming Bootcamp events and session timings.\n\nGET /api/areas/{city} \342\200\224 Returns all neighborhoods, Metro/Bus stops, and designated common meetup points for that city.\n\nPOST /api/commute \342\200\224 Submits or updates an attendee\'s choice (is_joining: True or False), area, transit stop, and boarding time using user_token.\n\nGET /api/commute/summary/{event_id} \342\200\224 Aggregates total attendees per area_id and boarding_time, returning:\n\nHeadcount per area/stop.\n\nList of attendee display names per cluster.\n\nThe generated Common Meetup Point instruction and Last-Mile Cab/Auto Split recommendation from nearest_venue_stop.\n\n2. Frontend Integration (Connecting the Stitch UI)\n\nWire the exported Stitch React components to the FastAPI endpoints with real-time state updates:\n\nPersistent Session Without Login Friction:\n\nGenerate a user_token (UUID) in localStorage on first visit so attendees can return later and modify their selection (YES \342\206\224 NO, change area, or adjust boarding time) without needing passwords.\n\nInteractive Decision Logic:\n\nClicking NO sends POST /api/commute with is_joining: false and renders the polite message: \"Hope you have your way figured out!\" alongside a \"Modify Selection\" button.\n\nClicking YES reveals the greeting \"It\'s a great event to learn and network!\", unlocks the Area, Metro/Bus Stop, and Boarding Time selectors, and dynamically queries /api/commute/summary/{event_id} to display how many people are coming from that exact area.\n\nEvent-Day Huddle Generator:\n\nOnce the user saves their YES plan, display the \"Common Point & Last-Mile Plan\" card showing:\n\nExact common meetup point at their origin Metro/Bus stop.\n\nFellow attendees joining from that area.\n\nStep-by-step last-mile instruction to deboard at the nearest venue stop and share a cab or auto together.\n\n3. Deliverables\n\nProvide:\n\nComplete requirements.txt (fastapi, uvicorn, sqlmodel, httpx, beautifulsoup4).\n\nComplete backend code (main.py) with pre-seeded Bengaluru & Gurugram transit hubs and live scraper integration.\n\nUpdated frontend code wired to the FastAPI endpoints with clean error handling and loading states.\n\nClear terminal instructions to run both the FastAPI server and frontend locally.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the html\n\nGoogle AI Studio Full-Stack Build Prompt\n\nYou are an expert full-stack Python and React developer. Take the exported UI prototype from Google Stitch and build a complete, runnable full-stack application for Bootcamp Commute Sync using a FastAPI backend and a React + Tailwind CSS frontend.\n\n1. Backend Requirements (FastAPI)\n\nCreate a clean, modular FastAPI backend (main.py) with CORS enabled and automatic Swagger UI (/docs):\n\nLive Event Scraper & Fallback (scraper.py):\n\nWrite an async function using httpx and BeautifulSoup4 to fetch https://promptwars.in/bootcamp.html.\n\nExtract upcoming Bootcamp cities (e.g., Bengaluru, Gurugram), session schedules (Morning Session: 9:00 AM - 1:00 PM, Evening Session: 2:00 PM - 6:00 PM), and program details.\n\nInclude robust fallback/seed data so the app works seamlessly even if the external page structure changes or is offline.\n\nDatabase & Models (models.py using SQLite + SQLModel):\n\nEvent: id, city, title, date_str, session_label, start_time, venue_area, nearest_venue_stop.\n\nCityArea: id, city, area_name, transit_stop, transit_type (Metro | Bus), common_meetup_point. (Pre-seed realistic areas and transit stops for Bengaluru and Gurugram).\n\nCommuteRSVP: id, user_token (unique UUID string), attendee_name, event_id, area_id, boarding_time, is_joining (boolean), updated_at.\n\nREST API Endpoints:\n\nGET /api/events \342\200\224 Returns upcoming Bootcamp events and session timings.\n\nGET /api/areas/{city} \342\200\224 Returns all neighborhoods, Metro/Bus stops, and designated common meetup points for that city.\n\nPOST /api/commute \342\200\224 Submits or updates an attendee\'s choice (is_joining: True or False), area, transit stop, and boarding time using user_token.\n\nGET /api/commute/summary/{event_id} \342\200\224 Aggregates total attendees per area_id and boarding_time, returning:\n\nHeadcount per area/stop.\n\nList of attendee display names per cluster.\n\nThe generated Common Meetup Point instruction and Last-Mile Cab/Auto Split recommendation from nearest_venue_stop.\n\n2. Frontend Integration (Connecting the Stitch UI)\n\nWire the exported Stitch React components to the FastAPI endpoints with real-time state updates:\n\nPersistent Session Without Login Friction:\n\nGenerate a user_token (UUID) in localStorage on first visit so attendees can return later and modify their selection (YES \342\206\224 NO, change area, or adjust boarding time) without needing passwords.\n\nInteractive Decision Logic:\n\nClicking NO sends POST /api/commute with is_joining: false and renders the polite message: \"Hope you have your way figured out!\" alongside a \"Modify Selection\" button.\n\nClicking YES reveals the greeting \"It\'s a great event to learn and network!\", unlocks the Area, Metro/Bus Stop, and Boarding Time selectors, and dynamically queries /api/commute/summary/{event_id} to display how many people are coming from that exact area.\n\nEvent-Day Huddle Generator:\n\nOnce the user saves their YES plan, display the \"Common Point & Last-Mile Plan\" card showing:\n\nExact common meetup point at their origin Metro/Bus stop.\n\nFellow attendees joining from that area.\n\nStep-by-step last-mile instruction to deboard at the nearest venue stop and share a cab or auto together.\n\n3. Deliverables\n\nProvide:\n\nComplete requirements.txt (fastapi, uvicorn, sqlmodel, httpx, beautifulsoup4).\n\nComplete backend code (main.py) with pre-seeded Bengaluru & Gurugram transit hubs and live scraper integration.\n\nUpdated frontend code wired to the FastAPI endpoints with clean error handling and loading states.\n\nClear terminal instructions to run both the FastAPI server and frontend locally.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_28a89f8d.markdown. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
