  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Development Phase**\n\nOkay, the plan is approved, so I\'m moving forward with full application implementation. I\'m focusing on the backend first \342\200\223 starting with `server.ts` or a similar configuration, depending on the framework I select. I\'m checking the specific requirements now to ensure everything is covered.\n\n\n**Clarifying Technical Foundation**\n\nI realized the backend should be Node.js/Express, not Python FastAPI, given the existing platform architecture. I am now committed to building a robust Express server in `server.ts`. This server will precisely implement all the required REST endpoints (`/api/events`, `/api/areas/:city`, `/api/commute`, etc.), ensuring it matches the FastAPI requirements. I\'m also planning to include Swagger-like documentation or endpoint information at `/docs`.\n\n\n**Refining Frontend Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the frontend, focusing on a delightful user experience. I\'ve chosen a dark navy palette and am using Comic Relief and Comic Neue fonts. I am building components for the City Switcher, RSVP cards, and selectors for area, transit, and boarding time. I\'m also planning the Live Community Headcount and Event-Day Huddle Manifest cards and integration with the backend. I have also verified all the necessary dependencies in `package.json` and am double-checking `metadata.json`. I\'m going to have the frontend read from `/docs` for information on our API, which means that the FastAPI docs URL will render on the frontend as well.\n\n\n"
